# .envrc — direnv integration
#
# Automatically enters the Nix shell whenever you `cd` into this directory.
# Requires:  direnv (https://direnv.net/)   +   nix-direnv (recommended)
#
# Setup (one-time, per machine):
#   1. Install direnv:   nix-env -iA nixpkgs.direnv
#                     OR brew install direnv  (macOS)
#   2. Hook into shell:  echo 'eval "$(direnv hook zsh)"' >> ~/.zshrc
#                        (replace zsh with bash/fish as needed)
#   3. Allow this file:  direnv allow
#
# If you have nix-direnv (faster, cached):
#   use nix
#
# Plain nix-shell fallback (slower, re-evaluates every time):
use nix
